<title>ESTONIA: HOIUPANK SAYS INVESTMENT ARM TO START WORK.</title>
<headline>HOIUPANK SAYS INVESTMENT ARM TO START WORK.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Estonia's Hoiupank said on Friday that its subsidiary, Hoiupank Investment, would start work at the end of March.</p>
<p>The bank said in a statement that the investment subsidiary would organise stock market issues, work on privatisation and give business consultancy services.</p>
<p>The share capital of the investment unit is 500,000 kroons and Hoiupank is the sole owner.</p>
<p>-- Tallinn Newsroom +372 630 8400</p>
